\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Leave-one-subject-out jackknife: the 29 leave-one-out mean pre-calibration balanced accuracies obtained by excluding each subject from R2 in turn (see Supplementary Table S1). Reference lines mark the full-sample mean (0.5773 $\pm $ 0.0005), the null 95\% CI upper bound (0.5172 $\pm $ 0.0005), and the C4 null mean (0.4995). No exclusion drops the mean below the null CI upper bound; the extremes are sub-03 (highest, 0.5852 $\pm $ 0.0005) and sub-18 (lowest, 0.5703 $\pm $ 0.0005).}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:2}{{2}{5}{Leave-one-subject-out jackknife: the 29 leave-one-out mean pre-calibration balanced accuracies obtained by excluding each subject from R2 in turn (see Supplementary Table S1). Reference lines mark the full-sample mean (0.5773 $\pm $ 0.0005), the null 95\% CI upper bound (0.5172 $\pm $ 0.0005), and the C4 null mean (0.4995). No exclusion drops the mean below the null CI upper bound; the extremes are sub-03 (highest, 0.5852 $\pm $ 0.0005) and sub-18 (lowest, 0.5703 $\pm $ 0.0005)}{figure.2}{}}
